---
import { capabilities } from "../../css-capability-catalogue";
import ComparisonPage from "../../components/ComparisonPage.astro";
import ComparisonSection from "../../components/ComparisonSection.astro";
---
<ComparisonPage title="CSS capability comparisons">
    {capabilities.map(({ slug, name, Reference, Managed }) => <ComparisonSection slug={slug} name={name}>
      <table><thead><tr><th>Size</th><th>Motion reference</th><th>Public CSS icon</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{[14, 16, 24, 28].map(size => <tr data-pair data-size={size}>
          <th scope="row">{size} px</th><td><Reference size={size} controlled data-sample /></td><td><Managed size={size} controlled data-sample /></td>
        </tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
      <a href="#destination" data-parent><Managed /> Parent hover</a>
    </ComparisonSection>)}
    <p id="destination">Link destination</p>

  <Fragment slot="checks">

    <p>Seven public CSS icons share drawing and recipe data with fixture-only Motion references using the previous mechanisms. Checks cover group translation and rotation, delayed opacity on paths and rectangles, interruption, return, completion, and cleanup at 14, 16, 24, and 28 px. Matrix tolerance is 0.005; opacity tolerance is 0.001. Numerical results do not grant visual acceptance.</p>
    <button id="parity" type="button">Compare playback</button>
    <output id="parity-result"></output>
    <button id="runtime" type="button">Check synthetic lifecycle</button>
    <output id="runtime-result"></output>
    <p>The lifecycle probes dispatch synthetic pointer events and replace matchMedia temporarily. Real touch hardware and operating-system preferences require manual review.</p>
  </Fragment>
</ComparisonPage>

<script>
  import "../../css-capability-checks";
</script>
